no-row-check: the Python gate answered a missing row with the searched-paths
sentence ("no review_coverage event for this PR (searched: <state-root
paths>)"); the native read returns the unknown sentinel row instead of None,
so the same answer renders as the bare word ("coverage unknown"). The
searched list is also the state-root fingerprint: the port moved state from
the FNO_STATE_DIR convention to the agents-home convention, so the paths in
the sentence cannot match. The state and exit stay the contract; parity
compares exit, stdout, the stderr refusal word and the stub-call folds only
for this case.
